# Reviewing changes in `services/`

The unified reviewer (`prompts/codeReviewer/v3/`) loads **`services/REVIEW.md`** for any
changed path under `services/`. That map cites rule IDs from `services/AGENTS.md` (e.g.
`Invariant #4`, `AP-1`, `H1`, `TAP-2`) and root `AGENTS.md` (`Invariant #7`) — it never
restates the rule text.

Deterministic checks that fire here first (precedence over LLM):
- D1 dependency table (`check_dependency_rules`) — services must not import `components/`
  or `langgraph`/`langchain` (exception: `llm_config.py` wraps `ChatLiteLLM`).
- D5 anti-patterns (`detect_anti_patterns` AP-2/AP-3/AP-5/AP-6) including hardcoded prompts (AP-3).
- D3 TAP-2 mock abuse + TAP-4 failure-path ratio on `tests/services/**`.

Dispatch the reviewer:

```bash
python -m meta.code_reviewer --from-git-diff --git-base HEAD --prompt-version v3 --output review.json
```

Deterministic findings are the gate; the v3 LLM judge is WI-8 certified (TPR/TNR = 1.0) so LLM verdicts are gate-grade for the routed LLM-only rules — re-record when the judge model changes.
Full contract: `docs/skills/code-review/SKILL.md`.
